Subject: [PATCH] fix gcc-15 format, enum and qualifier diagnostics

Remaining -Wall diagnostics in the vendor tree, plus one memory-safety bug
they exposed:

 - cmm_info.c/rrm.c/rrm_tlv.c: kernel 6.6.y now defines MIN() in
   include/linux/minmax.h, so the local macros collide with it. #undef first
   and keep the vendor definition; behaviour is unchanged.
 - cmm_cfg.c: Set_PS_Flush_Proc() fed &MacTab.fPsSTAFlushEnable (BOOLEAN),
   &PsFlushThldTotalMsduNum and &PsFlushPerStaMaxMsduNum (UINT16) to
   sscanf("%d"), which writes four bytes each and clobbered the adjacent
   MacTab fields. Parse into INTs and assign with the right width.
 - hdev_ctrl.c: hc_set_mac_cap()/hc_set_phy_cap() were defined with UINT32
   while hdev_ctrl.h declares enum MAC_CAP/PHY_CAP. Same width; match the
   prototype.
 - ap_cfg.c: CurrentState is an enum WNM_NOTIFY_STATE but was seeded from
   enum WNM_NOTIFY_EVENT. WAIT_WNM_NOTIFY_REQ is the same value (0).
 - mt7981.c: rx_fe_def[] initialises a struct whose only member is an array,
   so it needs a second level of braces.
 - rt_linux.h/rt_main_dev.c: dev_addr is const in this kernel; restore the
   vendor's UCHAR * view.
 - fwdl_mt.c: the fortify memmove builtins reject a volatile destination.

Deliberately left alone: the RTMP_OS_TASK_CALLBACK and get_wireless_stats
function-pointer casts (compat shims), and the vendor MIN() macros that
actually compute the maximum.

diff -ru a/mt_wifi/chips/mt7981.c b/mt_wifi/chips/mt7981.c
--- a/mt_wifi/chips/mt7981.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/chips/mt7981.c
@@ -1285,7 +1285,7 @@
 #if defined(CONFIG_WLAN_SERVICE)
 static struct _rx_fe_loss_ee_def rx_fe_def[] = {
 	/* adie 7976 */
-	{ 0x3f6, 0x3f7, 0x3f8, 0x3f9,  /* 2G */
+	{ { 0x3f6, 0x3f7, 0x3f8, 0x3f9,  /* 2G */
 	  0x3fa, 0x3fd, 0x400, 0x403,  /* 5G LB */
 	  0x3fb, 0x3fe, 0x401, 0x404,  /* 5G LM */
 	  0x3fc, 0x3ff, 0x402, 0x405,  /* 5G LH */
@@ -1293,7 +1293,7 @@
 	  0x407, 0x40b, 0x40f, 0x413,  /* 6G LB2 */
 	  0x408, 0x40c, 0x410, 0x414,  /* 6G HB1 */
 	  0x409, 0x40d, 0x411, 0x415   /* 6G HB2 */
-	 }
+	 } }
 };
 
 static UINT32 mt7981_get_rx_fe_loss(
